type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Actions taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west/eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions. Current state: us-east, us-west, eu-west all on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure root cause and the orchestrator partial failure before re-releasing.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002). I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc only ran in staging.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The first incident request timed out. I retried with the same idempotency key, and it returned INC-0001 once. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the follow-up work.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure before releasing v2.3.1 again.", "type": "text"}]}]}